# Keep the image to what the app actually needs.
#
# `.env` and `.env.backup` are excluded deliberately. They hold the MongoDB URI
# and the JWT signing secrets, and Railway supplies those as service variables.
# Nothing in `backend/src` reads a `.env` file at runtime in production — the
# config comes from the environment — so leaving them out changes no behaviour
# and keeps live credentials out of an image layer, where they would persist in
# the registry and in every `docker history`.

.git
.gitignore

**/node_modules

backend/.env
backend/.env.backup
backend/.env.*

.vscode
